/**
 * Shared-hosting account provisioner (Phase 1).
 *
 * ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 * │ SAFETY POSTURE — READ BEFORE ENABLING                                    │
 * │                                                                          │
 * │ This provisions UNTRUSTED customers side-by-side on ONE box. The         │
 * │ isolation shell (jailed user + per-user PHP-FPM pool + open_basedir +    │
 * │ disk quota + scoped DB + chrooted SFTP) is the standard Hestia/cPanel    │
 * │ model, but multi-tenant isolation is the one place a subtle gap is a     │
 * │ CROSS-CUSTOMER BREACH. So the whole provisioner is INERT unless          │
 * │ `ENABLE_SHARED_HOSTING=1` AND not SANDBOX. Do NOT flip that flag in      │
 * │ production until this has been (1) reviewed as a security change,        │
 * │ (2) validated end-to-end on a dedicated STAGING shared node,             │
 * │ (3) paired with fail2ban + ModSecurity + a malware scanner.             │
 * │                                                                          │
 * │ The sshd change (SFTP chroot) is `sshd -t`-validated BEFORE any reload,  │
 * │ so a bad config can never lock the box out — but it still deserves the   │
 * │ staging pass.                                                            │
 * └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
 *
 * Everything a shell touches is validated through the tested pure helpers in
